[{:db/id "q-117890/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "3f8e3591-f142-5c76-b105-ed69de29e552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "1a7453a2-6775-5dfa-ba33-6a9e13793dc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "5f99a275-8a84-5c4a-8449-1378c5866969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "c1416dc0-034f-5156-9145-6ffddd35b063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "d3700295-4eef-5aaa-a686-b739de422da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00abf91d-e490-52e0-990b-e86391d300fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117890/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer-field/choices ["q-117890/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-117890/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" "q-117890/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-117890/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-117890/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117890" :question/id #uuid "6977be63-f7d9-5402-9e3e-ed4149021972" :question/math-academy-id "q-117890" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/d54c590d8d64670c0fb90baea864d154cb4c59cd69d7f57234bfd8a5c4a3bfe7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}(x+4C))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+4C$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}(x+4C))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/336c38a44a3a40fcaf4a226f61a9f7af2cc731674c1ccc6679b80d846d4ea657.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})$ by $0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ units to the left. Therefore\n\n$$\n4C=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117890/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117890"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "cdf87fd1-f795-5640-8860-ef91fcf2092e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9db5fa0a-5a66-50d6-9d73-ebf01c32d110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0881f3e4-e1db-5b0d-91fe-b8b5e1a34b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "119a7ffa-aa3f-59e9-985e-7361d5667cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "69b40c59-c946-537e-9080-234210d2d2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd06d8d3-4017-5da2-b399-f066dc028bfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141999/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-141999/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-141999/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-141999/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-141999/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-141999/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141999" :question/id #uuid "b85652aa-105e-56e5-bee4-742b27b9d838" :question/math-academy-id "q-141999" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/8b237f9e857b1ed87de447aa79c14d359429e71d8afe7ab8eab201eba7ffb6af.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is  $B+2D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}=2.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Therefore, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+2D=2+2\\cdot (1)=2+2=4.$  \n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "5d759a0e-76f7-547c-bb28-27a23d3b0dfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "09a361bb-0e13-5df4-bd4e-5fe5f2ce04cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "78436634-6e1a-58d8-ac34-23b32dfebcdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1cecb0d4-8a59-5e36-a009-78c68c45cb83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "2cf54403-84cf-5b35-845a-8f068ff7067a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a78e2d19-7dec-52f4-96d0-14d0ff65a95f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143666/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-143666/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-143666/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-143666/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-143666/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-143666/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143666" :question/id #uuid "9cef5111-5a4a-58fb-8dde-16bb9670ea94" :question/math-academy-id "q-143666" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/148ef6b6d54262df159703437a6003e8f884052b98e95eb61536890a987a07f1.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B-D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{9}{4}$ units up. Hence, $D=\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, $B-D=\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{9}{4}=-1.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143666/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" :answer/id #uuid "05d1cab4-a517-57e7-8455-7aea2ec8b78e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "3bffd968-2c0a-51d6-a679-3ed68c880dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "ea6ac96a-4062-5f53-8a70-fc35e6b07148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection/37d04d9504e3dd5572231cf73505026821eeb93b1f1f5d805ea72efcab2d0843" :answer/id #uuid "010d9895-c354-5b20-bc2f-e74894160f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "ec72af4d-6d28-5d0a-88e1-91c144c71c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c52f41ed-d7f4-5ae3-9bd5-920d44dd7105" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143672/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-143672/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" "q-143672/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-143672/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" "q-143672/selection/37d04d9504e3dd5572231cf73505026821eeb93b1f1f5d805ea72efcab2d0843" "q-143672/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143672" :question/id #uuid "2c0dbf5f-c695-5305-b340-7d3b320f640f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143672" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/6a90f799d2dfd2dbd971e15eb195f4109ab7b6ceb204943a8ed2fd6c83bb620c.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+2C$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}(x+2C))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=cot\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/0e94fbec60ae4d47d3a4fba50f8a875d9bb3938776940cc9688413d2cb22aa9e.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ units to the left. Therefore:\n\n$$\n2C=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143672/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection/86ae4adf744f83815c6e176da09d1e1a7388c41a2337e3e7a6825862a8a438ec" :answer/id #uuid "98823927-f09f-5292-b5b4-acd26588785a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "568fa9eb-24da-5469-9988-8a4c15038694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" :answer/id #uuid "cff66501-f17e-5848-81ab-f6b798cc4916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "a619f095-baf3-517e-9157-9a4b16bb84d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection/4f4832c36defb1ed86287b2874a58927849dd3eb93f2306b966c53090e40ee49" :answer/id #uuid "2a70298f-5e45-53e6-bc9e-3fff233e8071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "801996a9-63df-5cb7-9431-6c5a4a169b57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143676/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-143676/selection/86ae4adf744f83815c6e176da09d1e1a7388c41a2337e3e7a6825862a8a438ec" "q-143676/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-143676/selection/751c07c835941eaca31781573c15b06b9426f5f2f4241ac45abc1c25f7716c0d" "q-143676/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" "q-143676/selection/4f4832c36defb1ed86287b2874a58927849dd3eb93f2306b966c53090e40ee49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143676" :question/id #uuid "6755a1e6-595a-542c-9f22-c873f4cb8de6" :question/math-academy-id "q-143676" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/0f994407d304e5b1105aeef37a62d6d51bcad43e76757846e0b42b8f257024b3.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5}+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5}+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}(x+\\frac{5C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{5C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}(x+\\frac{5C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5}).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949463/assets/1b3e3365d8047befbe70c2371a44e61262c68a2da694ab410ae974917e8535bd.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})$ by $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ units to the right. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5C}{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,C=(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})(\\frac{2}{5})\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{5}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $-\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143676/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
